# cursword_fsm.c's real, table-driven state graph. H-AI-LAB-DESIGN.md
# Part 2: this replaces the old plain-procedural set_state("X") shape
# (no table, no validation - the whole reason cursword couldn't be
# the AI registry's first real fsm-kind entry, or show up in an
# event-shaped viewer). Every real edge below is the exact transition
# sequence already live in run_onboarding()/main() - see ops/README.md
# "States" section for the human-readable walk. cursword_fsm.c now
# loads this table at startup and validates every set_state() call
# against it (WARN + still-allow on a genuinely new/unlisted edge -
# never hard-fail a working onboarding flow over a table mistake, but
# never silently accept an edge without a trace either).
#
# STATE | <name> | NEXT=<comma-separated allowed next states>
# "(start)" is the pseudo-state for the FSM's own two real entry
# points - not a real state cursword_fsm.state is ever written as.
STATE | (start)       | NEXT=OFFER,IDLE
STATE | OFFER          | NEXT=OPEN_USER
STATE | OPEN_USER      | NEXT=NEW_USER,ERROR
STATE | NEW_USER       | NEXT=AUTO_ID,WATCH_SIGNUP
STATE | AUTO_ID        | NEXT=AUTO_NAME
STATE | AUTO_NAME      | NEXT=WATCH_DONE
STATE | WATCH_SIGNUP   | NEXT=WATCH_DONE
STATE | WATCH_DONE     | NEXT=IDLE,DONE
STATE | DONE           | NEXT=IDLE
STATE | ERROR          | NEXT=
STATE | IDLE           | NEXT=
